{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "_memo = [0, 0, 2, 0]\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < len(_memo):\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    for i in range(len(_memo), n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = _memo[i-1] + _memo[i-2] + _memo[i-3] + _memo[i-4]\n        _memo.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return _memo[n]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the cache with the first four base case values.\n    fib4_cache = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Iteratively calculate Fib4 numbers from the 4th index up to n.\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = fib4_cache[i-1] + fib4_cache[i-2] + fib4_cache[i-3] + fib4_cache[i-4]\n        fib4_cache.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return fib4_cache[n]"}
